pheonix_wrong: Please state your full name and profession to the court.
suspect1: I’m Dayton Attaquer. I don’t know why that witness insists on suspecting me! I didn’t even log in!
you: Oh?
pheonix_wrong: Mr. Attaquer, please give a full account of what you were doing the night Mr. Database was murdered.
suspect1: Yes! Ahem…
suspect1: I was at home that night, tucked in front of my computer.
suspect1: As someone who enjoys testing company websites in his free time, I like to submit bug reports to these websites when I find errors in their code or logic.
suspect1: I don’t understand why I’m suddenly suspected just for that! Apparently all these companies I thought I was helping are gossipping about me.
suspect1: Anyway…
suspect1: I was just surfing the web. I… I found a new company website, and clicked, and investigated! As I always do! I had to log in before making a bug report, so I did!
suspect1: And then I was arrested, it’s ridiculous! Besides, user input, in a bug report of all things, can never affect a database! There’s not even any evidence that records were deleted!
you: (This testimony…)
